The easiest way is to have the user's mail handler (not sendmail) specify a
Reply-To header. At least this is easier than to study the 700+ pages in the
O'Reilly book about sendmail.

Seems like You are using an osf1 system (why else would You post to this
group). I assume You have checked the man page 'mail_manual_setup'. You
should try to stay with the DEC supplied macros (written by Paul Vixie).

That's a masterpiece of simplicity in the sendmail world. The macros from
Berkely and Berkeley's latest sendmail should allow You to do what You
want (see user database), but to my opinion they are a mess.

So keep it simple and stupid (and safe and working), and see if the Reply-To
header does what You need.

