>Please tell me what I am doing wrong, or tell me what else you need to
>know before you can help me.
>Thank you,
>Daniel (feeling frustrated) Minor
>
>
I presume that this must have worked at some point when you installed
the OS, or was it a FIS jobbie?

I know this is probably obvious and I trust that you've already tried
it, but I'll ask it anyway - are you doing this as superuser? If not
then try that. Otherwise check to make sure that the block special and
character special devices exist in /dev for your CD-ROM, they should
be rz4c and rrz4c respectively, both with major device number 8, minor
device number 4098. If they don't exist try using the /dev/MAKEDEV
utility. If one is missing then try using mknod to re-create it. Also
check that your kernel supports the device: there should be a line
that looks like:

device disk     rz4        at scsi0     drive     32

in your /sys/conf/KERNEL_PARAMETERS_FILE.

Good luck.



