In article <6367m6$fuq$1@charm.magnus.acs.ohio-state.edu>,
Michael T. Davis <DAVISM@er6.eng.ohio-state.edu> wrote:
>
>	A user here recently upgraded his DEC 3000/600 to dUNIX v4.0b.  When
>the system is started, it has trouble starting routed.  In particular, when
>/sbin/init.d/route is called, the following error message is displayed:
>
>routed: router/udp: unknown service

This usually indicates that routed can't find the entry in /etc/services
that should look like this:

route		520/udp		router routed		

Is this system getting services from /etc/services or via NIS?  If NIS,
the master is probably missing the above line and it will have to be
added to the master NIS services file and the map rebuilt.  You can
check /etc/svc.conf to see where services is coming from.


