>After I upgraded to 3.2g (last year) my Alpha2000/500 doesn't 
>automatically boot all the way.  It boots to single user - pound prompt - 
>and then continues only when CTRL-D is hit on the console.  Why is this? 
>Some cruel joke ?

Next time you are at the console prompt (>>>), type:

	>>> show boot_osflags

The reply should be "A" for "AUTOMATIC" boot. If it is not, the system
will default to single user mode. You can reset it with:

	>>> set boot_osflags A

I don't know why an upgrade would have changed this....

