Anne-Gael Inisan (inisan@afmb.cnrs-mrs.fr) wrote:
: Hello !

: This program creates a binary file, and my problem is that those two binary
: files (created one on SGI, the other on DEC) differ: I can't transfer the file
: from a machine to the other. That's a pain for my customers who have
: heterogenous networks.
: I already assumed that the alpha is a 64 bits machine, the SGI 32. The two
: binary files have the same number of bytes. I tried to 'swapbyte' one file
: as well.

: Can anyone explain me this ? Is there a solution ?

Try compiling your DEC executable with -convert big_endian.

Generally, you should *never* expect binary files to be compatible between
different machines (and even between different compilers on the same OS) -
unless you go to the (quite considerable) effort of designing your files
to be portable in the first place.

/Serge.P

