OK, before anyone goes to the trouble of replying to my query
from earlier this morning, I've found my answer.  No thanks to
Digital's online documentation ("man -k" didn't point me to an
appropriate manpage), but (as is often the case) I was able to
find the information I needed by browsing through back issues
of the alpha-osf-managers mailing list.

The executive summary:  This (mis)feature is new with DUnix V4;
it's part of the "power management subsystem".  By default, any
disk not accessed for twenty minutes gets spun down, allegedly
to save power.  (How much power does this really save, anyway?)

Fortunately, there's an easy way to disable this; "man dxpower"
tells how.  (And "man -k power" would have pointed me there, if
only I'd been able to guess what keyword would do the trick.)

