Beats me why it's doing it, but as an (ugly) work-around, how about just
running a process which reads a random block from the raw drive every
minute?  It's pretty gross, but it'll keep the idle timer (wherever it is)
from spinning the drive down, and the performance impact should be
minimal:

/* pseudocode */
fd = open ("/dev/rrzNc")
while(1)
{
   i = random (0, SIZE_OF_DISK)
   seek (fd, i)
   read (fd, buf, 512)
   sleep (60) /* or whatever it takes */
}

