>>  I loaded the 4.0c UNIX off the CD but I am still showing 4.0b ?
>>  Ummm..is this normal behaviour with Digital Unix upgrades or am I missing
>>  something here?

I asked a similar question back in August, and got a number of replies, all of
which basically said the same thing:

The 4.0c release *is* simply 4.0b, plus platform-specific hardware support for
the au-series personal workstations.  So if you install from the 4.0c CD onto
one of the au PWs, you get 4.0c; install onto anything else, and you get 4.0b.

