Hi Justus!

Since you already have a RAID 5 set going for you, you don't really need
to worry about individual failures. Therefore, I can't see any reason for
wanting to use LSM.

What I would do in your case is make one file domain, and chunk it up into
different filesets, enabling fileset quotas on each of the different
filesets so one runaway file can't ruin it all the other filesets

For making large filedomains, you'll also want to remember to use the -x
and -p options to mkfdmn, so that you don't run out of metadata space (as
well as not letting it get overly fragmented)

Also - be sure to have the latest patchkit installed (which is now
patchkit 5), which contains the advfs consolidated patch.

-Jay
