Hello!

I think your data on that external disk has been deleted when you created the new
file domain with mkfdmn.
You�d better created a symbolic link in the directory /etc/fdmns/domainname
(domainname = name of the AdvFS domain you created with mkfdmn).
That symbolic link should be named like your external disk, i.e. rz3, which
must point to the device file of the corresponding disk partition, i.e. /dev/rz3c.

Creating this symbolic link makes your AdvFS domain available without
touching your external disk.
Creating a new AdvFS domain with mkfdmn will overwrite the existing one.

I hope you�ve made a backup of your data!

Regards,

Juergen Luther.


