> or deny remote access form specified hosts or domains (i want to specify
> ip address) to OSF1 server? (something like hosts.allow and hosts.deny
> in linux). I have tried to find any info in the Digital UNIX
> documentation, but I haven't found anything...
> I am using Digital UNIX v.3.2 with C2 security installed.
>
> Greetz!
>     Pawel.

For remote telnet,rsh,rlogin,etc connections adjust
the /etc/hosts.equiv file. For ftp connections use the
/etc/ftpusers file. For X connections update the /etc/securettys
file and use the standard xhost command. The .rhosts and
and .netrc files are also present in OSF1.

  For security reasons these files must be carefully
updated.

All files have comments and are described in some detail in
man pages. Additional information about optional security
subsets and Security Integration Architecture can be obtained
in the DU Security manual.

Hope this helps.

Best Regards,

              Randolpho

