What I did to solve this problem was I renamed lpr to lpr.pro and created a
script  named lpr which sent 3 files to the printer using lpr.pro .  The
first print job simply had two pcl commands in it. One to set a carriage
return equal to a new line, the other to compressed text. The second  file
is the actual file to be printed. The third is a another PCL file that
resets the printer back to the defaults.  This works very well, however, I
have had some network print servers reset to default after every job, for
which the script does not work.  I usually have to set the printer up in
the printcap file to  :rp=text in these cases.  


Hope this helps....




