Ed Ady <adye@mail.dec.com> writes:

> Could some one please post why to use gzip instead of compress?
> Also, is there a problem with using compress/uncompress on files larger
> that 2GIG?

compress uses Lempel-Ziv compression which is far less effective than
the gzip algorithm. It's pretty old technology. It's also proprietary
and for that reason is missing from many Unix implementations. (Unisys
owns the rights to it.) gzip is free.

For just those reasons I don't see any reason to use
compress/uncompress. gzip is widely available, free, and works better.

If compress is properly implemented, the file size is not
relevant. (Of course, you need disk space for both the compressed and
uncompressed files for an instant unless you are piping the output
somewhere else.)
