I had problems when I first set up ppp on my Alpha Server as well.  First
of all,
You need to setup tty00 in the inittab with uugetty(You might already be
doing this).

I never was able to get ppp to automatically at first.  I would try dialing
in to the server  from a computer that is close to the server. Run pppd and
then look (  from a different computer of course) at the routing tables on
the server( netstat -r) and (ifconfig -a).  You should see a route list for
a ppp circuit.  I noticed when I first started messing with ppp that the
system would often have a route from and older ppp session. 

The other tip I have is that a modem, especially anything 28.8 or faster
require for the most part a chat script or at least an initializtion string
 set in modem's memory.  I once spent hours trying set up a Cisco dial on
demand router, thinking it was a routing problem when really it was a
problem with how I set up my modem. It had all the symptoms you have
described.  


For  USR 28.8 Sportster try inititializing  the modem up on the server with
this string:

at&f1&c1&d3m1&r2&b1&m4&k1&m0&k0


You can either write a chat script(recommended) or you save this to the
modem's memory.





