I've seen this before... I think I tracked it down to LSM not being 
configured in the kernel.  I think you need a couple of lines like:

pseudo-device 	lsm_ted	0
pseudo-device	lsm	1

in your /sys/conf/MACHINE_NAME

Then do a doconfig and a reboot and give it another go...

Andrew



