I suggest you use one or better two TZ89 DLT-Drives, so you can backup
the tablespacefiles in parallel.
You may use compression on Oracle-files, it gives typicaly a factor of
3 to 6. 
But since the TZ89 can handle about 3 Myte/s the tape sucks about
9 to 18 Myte/s or even more if compressing the Nulls in an empty
Oracle-file.
This is a very hard job for your disks and the SCSI-Bus.
So you should have a private SCSI-Bus for each TZ89 and using it
without compression helps the tape streaming.

Bye Matthias
