>     I have an AlphaStation on which I would like to set up a simple way
> to forbid interactive logins via the
> network (rlogin, telnet...) for a certain list of users. Until now
> I have found that /etc/nologin could be used
> to disallow logins ;  but I need a more selective way to do it. Have you
> any idea ?

If all of the remote users will come from machines that have or can have
an IDENT server, you can use extensions to TCP Wrappers to do this.  If
