Bruce Antolovich (bantolov@earthlink.net) wrote:
:  Hi,
: 
: Has anyone had success in mounting jaz disks under DU4.0B. I have read
: several archived postings which give instructions on proper disktab entries
: but after modifying disktab appropriately, I get unknown disk type messages
: when I try to disklabel. Some of the posts say that this is a problem with
: disklabel and should be fixed with patches from digital. Does anyone know
: which patch fixes disklabel sufficiently to let me mount the jaz disk. There
: is a jumbo patch which has everything (presumeably!) but since it is over
: 40MB, it is not exactly an easy download when using a modem.
: 
: If anyone could direct me to the correct patch or suggest a way to get this
: solved I would be very thankful.
: Sincerely,
: Bruce Antolovich
: bantolov@earthlink.net
: 

Don't expect a patch too soon.  DU4.0B's /usr/sbin/disklabel doesn't use
/etc/disktab!  DEC is pondering the inclusion of a switch to incorporate
the "old" behaviour in a future release.  To get a Jaz drive working on my
Alpha (DEC 3000 w/4.0B), a 3.2G disklabel was used.  It works like a charm!

See ddr.dbase (4) and ddr_config (8) for DEC's replacement for 
/etc/disktab.  Not surprisingly, most genuine DEC devices are already 
included in the ddr database.

Credit goes to Peter deFriesse; I am just reporting the results of his 
efforts.  Here is the disktab entry I am using:

jaz1|Iomega JAZ Drive:\
        :dt=SCSI:ty=removable:ns#32:nt#64:nc#1021:\
        :pa#15884:oa#0:ba#8192:fa#1024:\
        :pb#66880:ob#16384:bb#8192:fb#1024:tb=swap:\
        :pc#2091007:oc#0:bc#8192:fc#1024:\
        :pd#15884:od#376832:bd#8192:fd#1024:\
        :pe#307200:oe#393216:be#8192:fe#1024:\
        :pf#1390591:of#700416:bf#8192:ff#1024:\
        :pg#1714175:og#376832:bg#8192:fg#1024:\
        :ph#291346:oh#83968:bh#8192:fh#1024:

