Hi,
It depends on a quotacheck  bug.

When doing (as during boot by /sbin/init.d/quota)

quotacheck -a

the results (as seen by df) are wrong for file systems which in
/etc/fstab have the last number (fsck) greater than 1


DEC told me long time ago that the problem would have been
patched, but this has not yet done.

I see 2 Solutions:  

1)	put last number (fsck) in /etc/fstab to 1
	for each file system to be quota checked 
	
2)	change in /sbin/init.d/quota
	the instruction 	quotacheck -a
	in one quotacheck ....
	for each file system to be quota checked 

