CHAN SIU PANG wrote:
> 
> When I try to run the following, the computer give me the following
> error message.
> 
> DECthreads bugcheck (version V3.13-435), terminating execution.
> Failure initializing the manager thread tc

The quotas you've checked aren't usually the ones that cause problems
like this. More likely, you've exhausted either vm-vpagemax or
vm-mapentries, (/sbin/sysconfig -q vm will show you the settings). Raise
them (see man sysconfigdb). The defaults are pretty low, unfortunately,
and threads (stacks, in particular) are sensitive to these parameters in
currently released versions.

The default settings are:

vm-mapentries = 200
vm-vpagemax = 16384

For starters, try at least:

vm-mapentries = 32768
vm-vpagemax = 32768

