What exact version of DU 3.2 are you running? 3.2d and later include a patched
Tulip driver (i.e. driver for de-500 NIC) that fixes a problem just like the
one you're describing. Has to do with the FIFO threshold parameter that has to
be tuned upwards under increasing load to avoid misaligned packets.

I had the exact same problem about 2 years ago ( *before* that patch got
rolled into the distribution OS) and ended up getting the patch straight from
the Tulip driver programmer at DEC.

Of course if you're not using a DE-500 NIC, this is of no use to you. But,
hey, who knows?

Hope this helps.


