> disk as swap and you start the swap on cylinder 0.
> 
> Chuck Moore wrote:
> 
> > Hi,
> >
> > I have a RZ28D disk which is partitioned as follows:
> > > disklabel rz3c
> > ... (stuff removed) ...
> > 8 partitions:
> > #        size   offset    fstype   [fsize bsize   cpg]
> >   a:   131072        0    unused        0     0         # (Cyl.    0 - 95*)
> >   b:   401408   131072    unused        0     0         # (Cyl.   95*- 386*)
> >   c:  4110480        0    unused        0     0         # (Cyl.    0 - 2987*)
> >   d:  1191936   532480    unused        0     0         # (Cyl.  386*- 1253*)
> >   e:  1191936  1724416    unused        0     0         # (Cyl. 1253*- 2119*)
> >   f:  1194128  2916352    unused        0     0         # (Cyl. 2119*- 2987*)
> >   g:  1787904   532480      swap                        # (Cyl.  386*- 1686*)
> >   h:  1790096  2320384    unused        0     0         # (Cyl. 1686*- 2987*)
> >
> > Can I change the swap area to partition 'c' and use the whole disk as swap ?
> > (i.e. will I run into problems if I explicitly include cylinder 0 ? )
> >
> > -- Chuck

-- 

If you use cylinder 0 for the begining of the swap space it may 
overwrite your disklabel information which also contains the info that
the partition is a swap partition. You can use the whole disk as swap
partition but start it at cylinder 512 to be save - safe than sorry.

Joe



