The root partition on rz?a which starts on cylinder 0 DOES NOT overwrite
the disklabel information. The system knows to keep away from cyclinder
0 when the file system is created. As for a SWAP partition it is not
considered and the disklabel can be overwritten. In DU V4.x and up, I
believe there was some code put in the kernal system to steer clear
from cyclinder 0 - but not for earlier versions. You can actually see
the code in one of the system kernel files but I can not remember which
one to look at.

Joe



