> get an error saying "connection refused by server" or something to that
> effect.
> I know that in OpenVMS, you have to set up the securities on the local
> machine.  Is there something similar in UNIX? Is there something I need
> to set on the local machine? Does the /etc/securettys file have anything
> to do with it?
> 
> If anyone has any information, can you let me know.
> Thanks in advance.
> 
>   -vasu.

On the DEC UNIX server, you have to say where to export the window.
For example

   DISPLAY=ip:0.0
   export DISPLAY

where ip is the ip number of your local machine.

On your local machine, you have to allow the DEC UNIX server to display
a window on your machine. This can be done with the 'xhost' command.
For example

   /usr/bin/X11/xhost +name

where name is the name of the DEC UNIX server.

