  petergg@petergg.mincom.oz.au (Peter Golledge) wrote:
>
> After searching Digital man pages, html docs etc I can't find
> any reference to a keep alive timer for TCP on Digital UNIX.
> Does Digital UNIX have support for a keep alive timer for TCP?

The DU keep alive parameters are shortly described in the
file /usr/include/netinet/tcp_timer.h.

This parameters can be changed with the DU dbx utility.
For example, to change the tcp_keepidle parameter use the
following procedure as root:

# dbx -k /vmunix
dbx version 3.11.10
Type 'help' for help.

stopped at  [thread_block:2097 ,0xfffffc00002a8790]  Source not available

warning: Files compiled -g3: parameter values probably wrong


(dbx) p tcp_keepidle
14400
(dbx) patch tcp_keepidle = 1200
1200
(dbx) p tcp_keepidle
1200

(dbx) quit
#

The values are expressed in 0.5 seconds unit. So the default
value of 2 hours (14400) was adjusted to 10 min (1200).

The change take effect after the next reboot. Reconfiguring the
kernel return to the default values.

Hope this helps.

Best Regards 8-)

Randolpho

