Check the max_users setting in sysconfig, it is probably at 1024. Awhile
back we looked at increasing this, and called DEC. I got a long rambling
explanation (over the phone) about what would have to be done to change
this (i.e. reconfiguring the kernal) and why this would not be a good
idea (mostly that many other kernal params are based on this one, and
would also have to be reconfigured, i.e. lots of work to do).  
However, we were wanting to do this for a different reason. Our users
are assigned a Unix login in groups (10-50 users/login), so we only have
about 125 logins. We run approx 950 concurrent users, and were
anticipating an additional 50-100 background processes (to handle
printing and ftping). We have since found a way to reduce the background
processes to about 10, so we are still under the 1024 limit. Good luck.

If this is the case and you successfully do reconfig the kernal, could
you post the process to the newsgroup?
