"edge" <eds5@mail.idt.net> writes:

> Hello there -
> 
> Forgive me but I am rather new to this news group as well as system
> administration.  I was wondering if someone could tell me what the best
> method is to copying a file from VMS 6.0 (not OpenVMS - although I do have
> and OpenVMS v6.2 machine that may enter in to this equation) to Digital
> UNIX v3.2?  Should I do a VMS to OPENVMS copy and then use ftp (part of the
> UCX layered product on OpenVMS machine) to go to UNIX box?  I do I avoid
> data integrity/format problems of file?  Does OS account for this?

There is no difference between VMS and OpenVMS except the name. All
VMS since 5.2 is properly called OpenVMS by the silly marketing folks.

You can either install DECnet on the DU system and use dcp or install
an IP stack on the VMS system and use ftp. If you use UCX, you need to
decide if the transfer should be binary or ASCII. If you use another
stack (Process or Cisco), the formats are handled automatically.
